# Titania (titanium dioxide, TiO2) as a thin film: amorphous TiO2 grown by atomic layer
# deposition, 350 nm thick, measured by ellipsometry and spectrophotometry. Siefke et al.,
# Adv. Opt. Mater. 4, 1780 (2016), doi:10.1002/adom.201600250; data CC0 via refractiveindex.info
# (TiO2/nk/Siefke), resampled here to 5 nm. This is the index of TiO2 coatings (sputtered,
# evaporated, ALD, sol-gel and anodic films are amorphous or anatase, n 2.3-2.5 at 550 nm),
# not of the rutile crystal (n_o 2.65 at 550 nm). Strongly dispersive: 2.92 at 360 nm,
# 2.44 at 550, 2.34 at 830. The film's absorption is not carried (an index here is real):
# k = 0.029 at 360 nm, 0.004 at 380, under 0.001 from 400 nm up.
# aliases: tio2
